        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What is the best treadmill for walking and running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For most homes, the Horizon 7.0 AT: a 20 by 60-inch deck, 0.5 to 12 mph, 15 incline levels and a 325 lb limit, for about $935 on Amazon on 24 November 2026. The Schwinn 815 has the same deck size for about $900, and the Horizon 7.4 AT suits heavier or faster runners.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you use the same treadmill for walking and running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes, if it meets both users’ needs. The runner needs a belt of about 60 inches and a top speed of 10 to 12 mph; the walker needs a start speed of 1 mph or less and powered incline. Many treadmills meet one set of needs but not the other.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What size treadmill do I need for walking and running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A belt at least 55 inches long and 20 inches wide, and 60 inches long if the runner runs regularly or is tall. Walkers are usually comfortable on 50 inches, so the runner sets the length. A 22-inch width, as on the Horizon 7.4 AT, gives the most room.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a 55-inch treadmill long enough for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For jogging and moderate running, usually yes; for fast running or tall runners, 60 inches is more comfortable. The Sunny and WELLFIT picks here have 55-inch decks, and the other four have 60 inches.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What speed should a treadmill reach for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For most home runners, 10 mph (a 6-minute mile) is enough, and 12 mph (a 5-minute mile) gives headroom for sprint intervals. Five of our six picks reach 12 mph; the WELLFIT stops at 10 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which treadmill is best for a couple with different fitness levels?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One with a slow start speed, a 60-inch deck and saved profiles or app support. Sunny’s 15% auto-incline model stores three user profiles and has one-touch 3 and 6 mph buttons; the Horizon 7.0 AT and Schwinn 815 suit a couple using their own apps.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

